WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.412
Unit 2 is the guide's Step 1, the
landing-zone security baseline.

2
00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:06.912
It adds four things on
top of the landing zone.

3
00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:10.706
First, protect the hierarchy, with
the command from Learn's page,

4
00:00:10.706 --> 00:00:15.814
Protect your resource hierarchy: creating
management groups needs authorization,

5
00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:18.587
and new subscriptions
land in a default group.

6
00:00:18.587 --> 00:00:22.265
Second, assign the Microsoft
cloud security benchmark and the

7
00:00:22.265 --> 00:00:26.225
fed-ramp initiative at the intermediate
root, in do-not-enforce mode.

8
00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:29.550
Learn's Azure Policy assignment
structure page says that

9
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.875
mode evaluates compliance
without enforcing the effect.

10
00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:37.412
Keep it there for at least one
twenty-four-hour evaluation cycle

11
00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:41.350
and one compliance review with
the I S S O; Step 9 enforces.

12
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.600
Third, every hub resource sends
its logs to the workspace.

13
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.650
Fourth, Defender for Cloud on every
subscription, with continuous export.

14
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.975
Rollback is one command, deleting
the assignment, in minutes.

15
00:00:54.975 --> 00:00:57.174
Nothing at the root is excluded;

16
00:00:57.174 --> 00:01:00.790
exemptions come only through
Step 9, with an expiry.
